From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Duran <15650777+carlos-duran@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] BananaDS: local wireless Auto (wifi.local = auto)

A fourth mode beside off, host and join, not the default. Nothing happens until the game turns its wifi on (its
multiplayer menu, Download Play); then it listens for the hosts' beacons for 2 s plus up to 1 s at random and joins
a host of the same game (melonDS patch 0096's tag; one hosting by hand first, else the lowest address). Failing that
it joins a host that doesn't say its game (desktop melonDS) if there is no tagged one, or else hosts. Two that start
together both host: one alone in its session that hears, twice in a row, a host of the same game hosting by hand or
in Auto with a lower address, ends its session and joins that one. Nothing changes during a local wireless game. A
player whose host leaves looks again, and one of those left hosts. When the game turns its wifi off for 3 s of its
own time (it left its multiplayer mode; MKDS turns it off and on for under 2 s between its screens), Auto ends or
leaves its session and waits for the game's wifi again; the others look again. A game that goes online through
Nintendo WFC gets no session (its frames to the access point would also reach the session's players). Disconnect
holds Auto until the game turns its wifi off and on again.

wifi.local_auto_start = now (for tests) starts it without waiting for the game's wifi, and wifi.local_auto_test_wifi
scripts the game's wifi by frame. The log names each step, and who is in the session as people come and go.
